==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₁rewdʰ-}}
From {{bor|en|la|rubellus|t=reddish}}, diminutive of {{m|la|ruber|t=red}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₁rewdʰ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹuːˈbɛlə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rubella.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛlə|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{senseid|en|Q155857}}{{lb|en|pathology}} A mild disease caused by the {{taxlink|Rubella virus|species}} infecting the [[respiratory tract]], and characterised by a rash of pink dots, fever and swollen [[lymph node]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Sarah Lyall|title=Britain Tries to Quell Fear Over Vaccine for Children|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2002/02/10/international/europe/britain-tries-to-quell-fear-over-vaccine-for-children.html|date=2002-02-10|passage=At issue is the so-called MMR vaccine, which immunizes children against measles, mumps and '''rubella''', three potentially deadly diseases that were once common and have been mostly wiped out.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210214012209/https://www.nytimes.com/2002/02/10/international/europe/britain-tries-to-quell-fear-over-vaccine-for-children.html}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jessica Ravitz|title=Can forgotten rubella children of the ’60s hold clue for Zika babies?|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2016/09/08/health/rubella-house-zika-babies-future|date=2016-09-08|passage=They have congenital '''rubella''' syndrome, which they acquired during an outbreak of the '''rubella''' virus, or German measles.}}

